 ### Safety Rules
 
-- Always confirm with the user before running destructive commands: `project delete`, `trial start`
-- For mutations, verify the org/project context looks correct in the command output before proceeding with further changes
-- Never store or log authentication tokens — the CLI manages credentials automatically
+- Run mutations only when the user explicitly requests them. Treat issue state changes, assignments, merges, Seer analysis or plan generation, event submission, releases, deploys, uploads, project or alert changes, and non-GET `sentry api` requests as mutations.
+- Read the exact target first and verify its organization and project before mutating it.
+- Confirm the selected targets and expected impact immediately before destructive or bulk operations, including `project delete`, `release delete`, issue merges, and `trial start`.
+- Never use a search, inferred project, or unverified list result to select mutation targets unless the user explicitly requests a bulk operation and the selected count has been verified.
+- Never run `sentry auth login`, `sentry auth logout`, or `sentry auth token` unless the user explicitly asks. Limitless provides token-file authentication.
+- Never store or log authentication tokens.
 - If the CLI reports the wrong org/project, override with explicit `<org>/<project>` arguments
 
